{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Analytic necessary-and-sufficient parameter criterion\nThis gives an explicit integral condition in a,b,c for null-chain closure on the Minkowski ellipsoid. A global conformal-cylinder coordinate and a contour period identity compute the previously unnamed return-map translation. The criterion also proves a unique positive c for every prescribed positive rational winding ratio and gives an elementary formula when a=b.\n\nThe precise count matters: the GKT equator-return map has the displayed period criterion; a literal chain of full tropic-to-tropic arcs additionally requires **an even number of arcs**. Least periods and iterated closures are stated separately.\n\n## Independent review and scope\n- Separate adversarial geometry/source review: PASS_COMPLETE_ANALYTIC_CRITERION for the literal parameter-condition request\n- 2,087 submitted exact controls replay byte-identically; 752 independent exact diagnostics pass\n- The theorem and eight independent-review files are unchanged from the reviewed snapshots\n- GKT's classical invariant-density and Poncelet results are credited\n- This is an analytic criterion; no algebraic Cayley determinant or ordinary elliptic-torsion characterization is claimed\n- The imported torsion shortcut is corrected by an explicit third-kind pole/residue computation\n- Historical priority is unconfirmed, and there has been no human peer review\n\nSee unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/README.md and ANALYTIC_CRITERION.md. The frozen theorem's submission-time header is superseded by the completed review and release metadata. One substantive approach was used; the coordinating task owns the claimed_solved queue update.\n","files":[{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/QUEUE.md","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/ANALYTIC_CRITERION.md","additions":194,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/README.md","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/RESEARCH_LOG.md","additions":8,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/SOURCES.md","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/frozen_artifacts.json","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/prior_imported_report.json","additions":10,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/readiness.json","additions":10,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/REVIEW.md","additions":142,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/author_replay/ANALYTIC_CRITERION.md","additions":194,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/author_replay/verification.json","additions":34,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/author_replay/verify.py","additions":75,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/independent_checks.py","additions":97,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/independent_results.json","additions":26,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/review_summary.json","additions":25,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/review/source_verification.json","additions":27,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/source_manifest.json","additions":25,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/source_record.json","additions":45,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/status.json","additions":19,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/turns.jsonl","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/verification.json","additions":34,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/600008/verify.py","additions":75,"deletions":0}],"headRefName":"dot/math-600008","headRefOid":"4d8ba8e9438c9c8a463721adc1102dee821b11df","isDraft":true,"number":104,"state":"OPEN","title":"600008: analytic necessary-and-sufficient null-chain parameter criterion","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/104"}
